  .claude\skills\work\lessons.md:234:The relay fold's own first CI run sat queued for fifteen minutes without ever 
being assigned a
> .claude\skills\work\lessons.md:235:runner, and was then killed by the workflow's `timeout-minutes: 15` — reported as 
**`cancelled`**,
  .claude\skills\work\lessons.md:236:a word that reads like a human stopped it. Zero steps had executed. One re-run, 
no new commit, got
  .claude\skills\work\lessons.md:237:a runner immediately. Two things worth keeping: the classification test is *was a 
runner assigned
> .claude\skills\work\lessons.md:238:and did any step run*, not the word in the conclusion; and a watch that only asks 
"is it still
  .claude\skills\work\lessons.md:239:queued" learns nothing — measure the RUN, whose status and per-step conclusions 
are unambiguous.
  .claude\skills\work\lessons.md:240:
  .claude\skills\work\lessons.md:241:## Linear closing verbs — the post-mortem that closed a live item
  .claude\skills\work\lessons.md:242:
  .claude\skills\work\lessons.md:243:A merged PR's body read "the instruction that fixed AI4DEV-31's chain" — and 
Linear closed
  .claude\skills\work\lessons.md:268:fixes to its own findings — was deleted outright: *"I don't want confirmation 
drop it out now
  .claude\skills\work\lessons.md:269:and from the skill."* Why it lost its place: it re-checked material already 
covered three
  .claude\skills\work\lessons.md:270:independent ways (the verify suite proves the fixes run, luna re-executes before 
merge, the
  .claude\skills\work\lessons.md:271:required CI check gates the pinned head), and its wake choreography was the 
process's most
  .claude\skills\work\lessons.md:272:fragile part — on the first item it ran, both confirmation launches died silently 
with their
> .claude\skills\work\lessons.md:273:parent and stalled the item for hours while everyone watched files that would 
never appear.
  .claude\skills\work\lessons.md:274:Disposition authority was already the item agent's; confirmation had become a 
fourth check
  .claude\skills\work\lessons.md:275:that mostly manufactured waiting. Reviewers are now stateless — never resumed. A 
lost output is
  .claude\skills\work\lessons.md:276:re-run at the same pinned commit and said to be a fresh sample, not a 
reproduction. The resume
  .claude\skills\work\lessons.md:277:mechanics (pinning — including codex's sandbox pin, which on a resume is
  .claude\skills\work\lessons.md:278:`-c sandbox_mode=…` rather than the launch flag — run-header verification, 
session-store recovery,
  .claude\skills\work\reviewers.md:43:rationale lives here, in the part no reviewer reads.
