  .claude\skills\work\shared-invariants.md:31:Anthropic reports how much of each usage window is spent. 
`statusline.ps1` snapshots those
  .claude\skills\work\shared-invariants.md:32:numbers on every status-line refresh — the status line is the only place 
Claude Code delivers
  .claude\skills\work\shared-invariants.md:33:them, hooks get a different payload — and `loop/work/window-gauge.ps1` 
reads the snapshot and
  .claude\skills\work\shared-invariants.md:34:returns `OK`, `PAUSE` or `UNKNOWN`.
  .claude\skills\work\shared-invariants.md:35:
> .claude\skills\work\shared-invariants.md:36:- **The coordinator decides; nothing else may.** Read the gauge on 
**every** `FLOW` and `PULSE`
  .claude\skills\work\shared-invariants.md:37:  line. A second thing with authority to halt work is the same failure 
as a second way to close
  .claude\skills\work\shared-invariants.md:38:  work — and a brake inside an agent is one the founder cannot see.
  .claude\skills\work\shared-invariants.md:39:- **One line, and it is `PAUSE`** (founder 2026-08-06). There is no 
lower "start nothing new"
  .claude\skills\work\shared-invariants.md:40:  band. Such a band would have to be justified by what a sitting costs, 
which nobody has
  .claude\skills\work\shared-invariants.md:41:  measured, so it could only ever be a number that felt safe. Work 
starts whenever the gauge
  .claude\skills\work\shared-invariants.md:166:- Never judge a detached process's liveness from a process list — 
measure its own artifacts.
  .claude\skills\work\shared-invariants.md:167:- **Never launch a reviewer process from any role but 
`reviewer-runner`** (founder 2026-08-08).
  .claude\skills\work\shared-invariants.md:168:  One launcher is what keeps the recipes correct in a single place, 
makes reading stderr at launch
  .claude\skills\work\shared-invariants.md:169:  non-optional, and leaves an open gate addressable by agent id. It 
also puts every reviewer wait
  .claude\skills\work\shared-invariants.md:170:  on the wake channel that has not failed — a subagent's completion 
re-invokes its parent, whereas
> .claude\skills\work\shared-invariants.md:171:  the background shell watches it replaces went silent twice on one 
item.
  .claude\skills\work\shared-invariants.md:172:- PowerShell, never Bash. bun, never npm or pnpm.
