  .claude\skills\work\SKILL.md:97:   **A spawn prompt is item facts only.** It states what to RESOLVE, never a 
resolved value — no
  .claude\skills\work\SKILL.md:98:   chain, no parent, no label — and it never carries process instructions, because 
process lives
  .claude\skills\work\SKILL.md:99:   in the contracts and a spawn prompt is reviewed by nobody. One once told an item 
to queue
  .claude\skills\work\SKILL.md:100:   auto-merge at pull-request time, which would have merged it before a single gate 
ran; Gate 1
  .claude\skills\work\SKILL.md:105:   in the main checkout is invisible to the agent's own stamp — skip this and the 
founder's
  .claude\skills\work\SKILL.md:106:   supervision tree degrades to `AGENT AI4DEV-nn` with no parents, which is the one 
thing the
  .claude\skills\work\SKILL.md:107:   stamp exists to show. This is not a fact handed to the agent: it is the 
coordinator filing what
  .claude\skills\work\SKILL.md:108:   only the coordinator can read, where the hook will look for it.
  .claude\skills\work\SKILL.md:109:
> .claude\skills\work\SKILL.md:110:The conductor is born in the item's one worktree — the platform creates it at 
