  .claude\skills\work\SKILL.md:114:## While an item runs
  .claude\skills\work\SKILL.md:115:
> .claude\skills\work\SKILL.md:116:You receive one flow line per phase change and one completion. That is the whole of 
your
  .claude\skills\work\SKILL.md:117:involvement unless something asks for you.
  .claude\skills\work\SKILL.md:118:
  .claude\skills\work\SKILL.md:119:**Relay, never rule.** A question from an item reaches you verbatim and reaches the 
founder
  .claude\skills\work\SKILL.md:120:verbatim. You do not answer it, soften it, or decide it is unnecessary. Exactly two 
things are
  .claude\skills\work\SKILL.md:121:supposed to arrive: a finding that contradicts ratified text, and real scope growth.
  .claude\skills\work\SKILL.md:137:- **Two in one item means the design is not working** — say so plainly and propose 
the fix rather
  .claude\skills\work\SKILL.md:138:  than carrying the item on your back to the end.
  .claude\skills\work\SKILL.md:139:- **You still never write in the item's tree, rule on its content, or run its 
commands.** Rescuing
  .claude\skills\work\SKILL.md:140:  unpushed work after a confirmed death is the one exception, and it is recorded AS 
a rescue.
  .claude\skills\work\SKILL.md:141:
> .claude\skills\work\SKILL.md:142:**Fable out of credit** → tell the conductor to spawn `orchestrator-opus` for 
subsequent
  .claude\skills\work\SKILL.md:143:sittings, and say so in the report; the handoff is manual because 
`--fallback-model` never fires
  .claude\skills\work\SKILL.md:144:on billing errors. **A session limit is not out of credit** — it is the five-hour 
window, it is
  .claude\skills\work\SKILL.md:145:account-wide, and it heals itself. Never set a timer for the reset: it would fire 
into a
  .claude\skills\work\SKILL.md:146:credit-dead account, and a reset time already past rolls a full day.
  .claude\skills\work\SKILL.md:147:
